# Settings ▸ Privacy ▸ Data and onboarding's "Help improve Cra" row: with sharing on, the usage
# report and a new crash report reach the endpoint (the fixture server stands in for
# crabrowser.app); turned off, nothing goes out. The crash report is a made-up one in the
# throwaway home, written after the last look (sharing.json). What each report holds is
# CraCore's SharingTests.
home
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false, "shareUsageStats": true, "crashReports": "send"}
seed sharing.json {"crashesSeenUntil": "2001-01-01T00:00:00Z"}
crash-report ${FIXTURES}/CrashReports/Cra-2026-11-10-120000.ips
env CRA_SHARING_ENDPOINT=${ORIGIN}
expect-log sharing: stats on, crash reports send
cra://debug?sharing=stats
wait 2
expect-log sharing: usage stats sent
cra://debug?sharing=crash
wait 2
expect-log sharing: 1 new crash reports, send
expect-log sharing: crash report sent
# The same crash report isn't sent twice.
cra://debug?sharing=crash
wait 1
reject-log sharing: 2 new crash reports
# Off, as the onboarding row unticked: nothing is sent.
cra://debug?sharing=off
cra://debug?sharing=stats
wait 1
expect-log sharing: usage stats off, nothing sent
